{"name":"Crater Lake","hex":"#63797e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Crater Lake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Several lakes in Chugach Census Area, Copper River Census Area, Nome Census Area and Prince of Wales–Hyder Census Area and Juneau borough, Kodiak Island Borough, Matanuska-Susitna Borough and Yakutat borough, Alaska.","Three lakes in Coconino County, Arizona."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Crater_Lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Impact crater lake","blocks":[{"text":"An impact crater lake is a lake inside a depression caused by the impact of a meteor. It is also known as an annular lake in cases where the water body is shaped like a ring, as many impact crater lakes are."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Manicouagan-EO.JPG/330px-Manicouagan-EO.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impact_crater_lake"},{"title":"Volcanic crater lake","blocks":[{"text":"A volcanic crater lake, or simply crater lake, is a lake in a crater that was formed by explosive activity or a collapse during a volcanic eruption. Water from various sources accumulates in the crater to form the crater lake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gunung_rinjani.jpg/330px-Gunung_rinjani.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volcanic_crater_lake"},{"title":"Crater Lake","blocks":[{"text":"Crater Lake is a volcanic crater lake in south-central Oregon in the Western United States. It is the main feature of Crater Lake National Park and is a tourist attraction known for its deep blue color and water clarity. The lake partly fills a 2,148-foot-deep (655 m) caldera that was formed around 7,700 years ago\nby the collapse of the volcano Mount Mazama. No rivers flow into or out of the lake; the evaporation is compensated for by rain and snowfall at a rate such that the total amount of water is replaced every 150 years. With a depth of 1,949 feet (594 m), the lake is the deepest in the United States. In the world, it ranks tenth for maximum depth, as well as fifth for mean depth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Crater_Lake_National_Park_%282023%29.jpg/330px-Crater_Lake_National_Park_%282023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crater_Lake"},{"title":"Crater","blocks":[{"text":"A crater is a landform consisting of a hole or depression on a planetary surface, usually caused either by an object hitting the surface, or by geological activity on the planet. A crater has classically been described as: \"a bowl-shaped pit that is formed by a volcano, an explosion, or a meteorite impact\". On Earth, craters are \"generally the result of volcanic eruptions\", while \"meteorite impact craters are common on the Moon, but are rare on Earth\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Barringer_Crater_aerial_photo_by_USGS.jpg/330px-Barringer_Crater_aerial_photo_by_USGS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crater"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Siljan_WorldWind.jpg/500px-Siljan_WorldWind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Siljan_WorldWind.jpg/500px-Siljan_WorldWind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A satellite photograph of the Siljan Ring. Lake Siljan is a large part of the southwest edge of the much-eroded crater.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASiljan_WorldWind.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Lonar_Lake.jpg/500px-Lonar_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Lonar_Lake.jpg/500px-Lonar_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lonar Lake in India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALonar_Lake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Yak_Loum.jpg/500px-Yak_Loum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Yak_Loum.jpg/1280px-Yak_Loum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Yak_Loum.jpg/500px-Yak_Loum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lake Yeak Laom, Cambodia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYak_Loum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Hallasan_2.jpg/500px-Hallasan_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Hallasan_2.jpg/1280px-Hallasan_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Hallasan_2.jpg/500px-Hallasan_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baengnokdam crater lake of the mountain Hallasan in winter, South Korea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHallasan_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Toba_zoom.jpg/500px-Toba_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Toba_zoom.jpg/500px-Toba_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Landsat image of Lake Toba, Indonesia, the largest volcanic crater la